 <summary>Passkey compatibility</summary>
 <p>beam needs WebAuthn PRF, not just ordinary passkeys. PRF derives the key that encrypts your fleet directory. Support depends on the browser, operating system, passkey provider and sometimes the way a security key connects. The ceremony page checks browser capabilities, then verifies the selected passkey result.</p>
 <p>This is what vendors document, not a matrix beam has tested end to end. The browser’s encryption support and the passkey provider’s PRF support are separate requirements; unsupported or unverified combinations are not promised to work.</p>
 <table>
 <tr><th scope="row">Safari</th><td>For this page use Safari 18.4 or later. Safari 18.0 PRF support alone is insufficient.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Apple Passwords, iCloud Keychain</th><td>Use updated Apple software. iOS/iPadOS 18.4+ with Safari 18.4+ is the page’s practical baseline; macOS Safari 18.4+ also needs a compatible provider. <strong>Unverified:</strong> the oldest supported macOS and provider pairing, and whether Apple’s fix for PRF over a phone (hybrid) has shipped.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Firefox</th><td>Firefox 139+ on desktop has the browser features. Your passkey provider must still supply PRF. Firefox 130 alone is not enough to promise PRF. <strong>Unverified:</strong> Firefox on Android and iOS.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Chrome</th><td>Chrome 133+ meets the encryption baseline. PRF must still be confirmed for your provider. <strong>Unverified:</strong> the first Chrome release with PRF, and Google Password Manager’s PRF support by operating system and version.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">1Password for iOS</th><td>1Password for iOS 8.10.74+ adds provider PRF support on iOS 18. This page also needs Safari/iOS 18.4+ for X25519.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">1Password browser extension (beta 2.26.1), Android (beta 8.10.38)</th><td>PRF was introduced in these beta versions; earliest stable versions are <strong>unverified</strong> here. Update your provider and use the result check.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Security keys, YubiKey</th><td>Use a PRF-capable FIDO2 key with a browser/OS that exposes it. A key supporting hmac-secret alone does not guarantee WebAuthn PRF. <strong>Unverified:</strong> firmware and operating system minimums.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Windows Hello</th><td><strong>Unverified.</strong> Browser support does not imply Windows Hello support.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Bitwarden, Proton Pass, other providers</th><td><strong>Unverified.</strong> A provider that unlocks its own vault with PRF may still not return PRF for beam’s passkey.</td></tr>
 <tr><th scope="row">Edge, Samsung Internet</th><td><strong>Unverified.</strong> Chrome’s version numbers do not carry over; this page checks at runtime.</td></tr>
 </table>
